---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Mermaid from "../../components/Mermaid.astro";
import PageCards from "../../components/PageCards.astro";
import { nav } from "../../lib/nav";
import { url } from "../../lib/url";

const section = nav.find((s) => s.href === "/concepts/")!;

const architecture = `flowchart TD
  SRC["provider API<br>or a saved log file"]

  subgraph AD["providers/ — the only code that names a CI system"]
    SEG["segmenter.py<br>raw log → Section tree"]
    RSN["reasons.py<br>provider status → FailureReason"]
  end

  subgraph CO["core/ — provider-neutral, pure, offline"]
    PH["phases.py<br>Section → Phase"]
    ATT["attribution.py<br>WHICH PHASE FAILED"]
    DEN["denoise.py<br>strip · collapse · fold"]
    EXT["extract.py<br>matchers → windows"]
    BUD["budget.py<br>fit to max_input_tokens"]
  end

  EV[["EvidenceBundle<br>all the report step may see"]]

  subgraph OU["outputs"]
    REP["llm/report.py<br>deterministic report"]
    LLM["llm/ backend<br>explains WHY · optional"]
    RED["core/redact.py<br>scrub again"]
    REN["render/<br>terminal · md · json · MR note"]
  end

  SRC --> SEG
  SRC --> RSN
  SEG -- "core/ports.py — the only contract" --> PH
  PH --> ATT
  RSN --> ATT
  ATT -- "the blamed section, and only it" --> DEN
  DEN --> EXT
  EXT --> BUD
  BUD --> EV
  EV --> REP
  REP -. "redacted prompt" .-> LLM
  LLM -. "cause + fix, validated" .-> REP
  REP --> RED
  RED --> REN`;
---

<Base
    title="Concepts"
    description="How ci-doctor decides where a job failed, and what each part of the codebase does."
>
    <h1>Concepts</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        What the moving parts are called, what each one decides, and where it
        lives in the code. Read this section once and the <a
            href={url("/reference/configuration/")}>configuration&nbsp;</a
        >
        reference stops being a list of unexplained knobs.
    </p>

    <div class="note">
        <strong>The one rule everything else follows.</strong> Deterministic code
        decides
        <em>where</em> the job failed; the LLM only explains <em>why</em>. Phase
        attribution runs before any model is called, so a loud but harmless
        cache warning can never be blamed over the real <code>exit code 1</code
        >. If the classifier is wrong, that is a bug with a failing test — not a
        prompt to tune.
    </div>

    <PageCards pages={section.pages} />

    <h2>The shape of the whole thing</h2>
    <p>
        Where each module sits, and what actually flows between them. Note the
        two dotted edges: they are the only ones a model touches, and they carry
        evidence that has already been selected and redacted.
    </p>

    <Mermaid
        code={architecture}
        label="Architecture: provider adapters segment the log and normalise the failure reason; core assigns phases, attributes the failure, then denoises, extracts and budgets the blamed section into an EvidenceBundle; the report is built deterministically, optionally explained by a model, redacted, and rendered."
        caption="Solid edges are deterministic and offline. The dotted pair is the one optional model call."
    />

    <h2>The same code as layers</h2>
    <p>
        Three bands. Providers know their CI system and nothing else; core knows
        the domain and no provider; outputs render what core decided. The seam
        through the middle is the only way data crosses.
    </p>

    <div
        class="arch"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Architecture: provider adapters feed the provider-neutral core through ports; the core feeds the LLM and renderers."
    >
        <div class="band">
            <span class="band-label">Adapters</span>
            <div class="band-boxes">
                <span class="box">providers/gitlab/</span>
                <span class="box">providers/github/</span>
                <span class="box muted">providers/&lt;yours&gt;/</span>
            </div>
            <p class="band-note">
                REST client · log segmenter · failure-reason map
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="seam">
            <span class="seam-label">core/ports.py — the only contract</span>
        </div>

        <div class="band accent">
            <span class="band-label">Core (provider-neutral)</span>
            <div class="band-boxes">
                <span class="box">models</span>
                <span class="box">phases</span>
                <span class="box">attribution</span>
                <span class="box">denoise</span>
                <span class="box">extract</span>
                <span class="box">budget</span>
                <span class="box">redact</span>
            </div>
            <p class="band-note">
                Pure. No network, no clock, and no provider ever named here.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="seam">
            <span class="seam-label"
                >EvidenceBundle — all the report step is allowed to see</span
            >
        </div>

        <div class="band">
            <span class="band-label">Outputs</span>
            <div class="band-boxes">
                <span class="box">llm/ <span class="opt">optional</span></span>
                <span class="box">render/terminal</span>
                <span class="box">render/markdown</span>
                <span class="box">render/json</span>
            </div>
            <p class="band-note">
                With no model, the deterministic report is the output — not a
                stub.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
        <strong>Why the middle band is sealed.</strong>
        <code>grep -ri gitlab ci_doctor/core/</code>
        must return nothing, and CI fails if it does. That is what makes adding a
        CI system a matter of dropping in a directory rather than threading a third
        case through the classifier. <a href={url("/concepts/code-map/")}
            >The code map&nbsp;</a
        > walks it file by file.
    </div>

    <h2>The invariants</h2>
    <p>
        These are enforced by tests, not convention. The first three are
        load-bearing:
    </p>
    <ul class="tight">
        <li>
            <strong>The LLM never selects the failure phase.</strong> Attribution
            is deterministic and auditable.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>No provider identifiers in <code>core/</code>.</strong> Checked
            by grep in CI.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Always <code>exit 0</code>.</strong> ci-doctor can never change
            your pipeline's outcome or mask the real failure.
        </li>
        <li>
            Nothing reaches the public internet by default — no telemetry, no
            update checks, no runtime downloads.
        </li>
        <li>
            Never emit unredacted log content: redaction runs on the prompt <em
                >and</em
            > the report.
        </li>
        <li>
            Every truncation is visible (<code>… [N lines elided] …</code>),
            never a silent cut.
        </li>
    </ul>
</Base>

<style>
    .arch {
        margin: 1.75rem 0;
    }

    .band {
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: var(--card);
        padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    }
    .band.accent {
        border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, var(--border));
        background: var(--accent-soft);
    }

    .band-label {
        display: block;
        font-size: 0.74rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        color: var(--muted);
        margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }

    .band-boxes {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.4rem;
    }

    .box {
        font-family: var(--mono);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        padding: 0.32em 0.7em;
        border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--fg);
        white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .box.muted {
        color: var(--muted);
        border-style: dashed;
    }
    .box .opt {
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-size: 0.85em;
        color: var(--muted);
    }

    .band-note {
        margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        max-width: none;
    }

    /* The arrow joining two bands, with the contract that crosses it. */
    .seam {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 0.6rem;
        padding: 0.5rem 0;
        position: relative;
    }
    .seam::before,
    .seam::after {
        content: "";
        flex: 1;
        height: 1px;
        background: var(--border-strong);
    }
    .seam-label {
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        text-align: center;
        padding: 0 0.2rem;
    }
</style>
